300: ## 4. Application State & Concurrency Model (`src/state.rs`)
301: 
302: ### 4.1 State Structure
303: `AppState` is thread-safe, cheaply cloneable (`Arc`), and encapsulates the active flight dataset alongside the WebSocket broadcast bus:
304: 
305: ```rust
306: use std::sync::Arc;
307: use tokio::sync::{broadcast, RwLock};
308: use flightreader_export::model::FlightDataset;
309: use crate::lib::ServerConfig;
310: use crate::routes::ws::WsScrubMessage;
311: 
312: /// Shared application state across all request handlers and WebSocket connections.
313: #[derive(Clone)]
314: pub struct AppState {
315:     /// In-memory active flight dataset, protected by an asynchronous read-write lock.
316:     pub dataset: Arc<RwLock<Option<FlightDataset>>>,
317:     /// Immutable server launch configuration.
318:     pub config: Arc<ServerConfig>,
319:     /// Broadcast channel for real-time timeline scrubber synchronization (capacity: 128).
320:     pub ws_broadcaster: broadcast::Sender<WsScrubMessage>,
321:     /// Timestamp when server was started.
322:     pub start_time: std::time::Instant,
323: }
324: 
325: impl AppState {
326:     /// Creates a new `AppState` instance initialized from the given configuration.
327:     pub fn new(config: ServerConfig) -> Self {
328:         let (ws_broadcaster, _) = broadcast::channel(128);
329:         let dataset = Arc::new(RwLock::new(config.initial_dataset.clone()));
330:         
331:         Self {
332:             dataset,
333:             config: Arc::new(config),
334:             ws_broadcaster,
335:             start_time: std::time::Instant::now(),
336:         }
337:     }
338: 
339:     /// Convenience helper to set the active dataset and broadcast an update event.
340:     pub async fn set_dataset(&self, new_dataset: FlightDataset) {
341:         let count = new_dataset.points.len();
342:         let duration = new_dataset.metadata.duration_seconds;
343:         let log_type = new_dataset.metadata.log_type.clone();
344: 
345:         {
346:             let mut lock = self.dataset.write().await;
347:             *lock = Some(new_dataset);
348:         }
349: 
350:         let _ = self.ws_broadcaster.send(WsScrubMessage::DatasetLoaded {
351:             total_points: count,
352:             duration_seconds: duration,
353:             log_type,
354:         });
355:     }
356: 
357:     /// Checks if a dataset is currently loaded.
358:     pub async fn has_dataset(&self) -> bool {
359:         self.dataset.read().await.is_some()
360:     }
361: }
362: ```
363: 
364: ### 4.2 Concurrency & Deadlock Prevention
365: - All dataset reads (`read().await`) take read-locks that release immediately once data is cloned or summarized into response buffers.
366: - Dataset updates (`write().await`) occur only during the upload endpoint lifecycle. Writing takes $<10\ \mu\text{s}$ because `Option<FlightDataset>` pointer swap is atomic in memory.
367: - No locks are held across I/O awaits or WebSocket sends, guaranteeing zero deadlock conditions.
