901: To strictly enforce the zero-cloud invariant and prevent any DNS leaks, external font requests, or unauthorized telemetry tracking, all HTTP responses from `flightreader-server` inject the following authoritative CSP header:
902: 
903: ```http
904: Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' data:; connect-src 'self' ws:; img-src 'self' data: blob:; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
905: ```
906: 
907: ### 7.3 Security Defense-in-Depth Headers
908: In addition to CSP, the server attaches:
909: - `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` (prevents MIME sniffing exploits).
910: - `X-Frame-Options: DENY` (prevents clickjacking attacks).
911: - `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` (prevents path leakage).
912: - `Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()` (disables hardware sensors).
